  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nWhen authors use the new customizable select (`appearance: base`), they want to include rich HTML inside an `<option>` (such as icons, badges, or complex text formatting). However, they also need to provide a clean, plain-text fallback string for browsers or platforms that do not yet support `appearance: base` and fall back to `appearance: auto`.\n\nBeyond browser support limitations, this fallback is also important for intentional device-specific strategies. For example, an author may choose to use the native platform picker (`appearance: auto`) on mobile and other devices for accessibility, while opting into `appearance: base` on desktop.\n\nCurrently, when a label attribute is present, browsers use it to completely replace the content of the option. In `appearance: base`, this behavior wipes out the rich inner HTML inside `<option>`. As a result, authors cannot use the label attribute to provide a clean string for platform pickers without destroying their custom layout in `appearance: base`.\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\nTo achieve a clean platform-picker fallback alongside a custom layout today, authors must resort to complex workarounds:\n\n* Markup Duplication: Maintaining two separate `<select>` elements or duplicating `<option>` lists in the DOM, then hiding them conditionally using `@supports (appearance: base)` or JavaScript.\n* Fragile HTML Structuring: Omitting the label attribute entirely and forcing the inner rich HTML to rely on the browser's automatic text-content extraction algorithm. This is incredibly restrictive for complex layouts.\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\n### In appearance: auto\n\n* `<option>`: Render the label attribute value by default. If the label value is empty, render the `<option>` content.\n* `<optgroup>`: Render the label attribute value by default. If the label value is empty, render `<legend>` content.\n\n### In appearance: base\n\n* `<option>`: Render the content by default. If the element is empty (`:empty`), render the label value.\n* `<optgroup>`: Render `<legend>` by default. If no `<legend>` is present, render the label value.\n\n### Anything else?\n\nBy my understanding this is not too dissimilar from what UAs already do. In this [test page](https://codepen.io/sb3nder/full/vExgzbV) the current implemented behavior can be visualized:\n\nFor each test case, the resulting text is prefixed by the test type number:\n1. label attribute, empty `<option>`, no `<legend>`.\n2. **label attribute, `<option>` and `<legend>` content.**\n3. no label attribute, `<option>` and `<legend>` content.\n4. empty label attribute, `<option>` and `<legend>` content.\n\n```html\n<optgroup label=\"1. optgroup-label\">\n\t<option label=\"1. option-label\"></option>\n</optgroup>\n\n<optgroup label=\"2. optgroup-label\">\n\t<legend>2. optgroup-legend-content</legend>\n\t<option label=\"2. option-label\">2. option-content</option>\n</optgroup>\n\n<optgroup>\n\t<legend>3. optgroup-legend-content</legend>\n\t<option>3. option-content</option>\n</optgroup>\n\n<optgroup label=\"\">\n\t<legend>4. optgroup-legend-content</legend>\n\t<option label=\"\">4. option-content</option>\n</optgroup>\n```\n\nFor `<select>`:\n\nChrome: \n\n<img height=\"250\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/83b35cdb-3b0b-4781-90ad-c37e13166e3b\" />\n\n<img height=\"250\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4d5340b7-6c26-445a-a84f-c1d0f67229b9\" />\n\n<img height=\"250\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/fb61f942-1d95-44f0-a3b3-9933c61764a7\" />\n\nFirefox:\n\n<img height=\"250\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/51d3b9d2-a52b-4a8d-b66f-7984151bbdc0\" />\n\n<img height=\"250\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bffe1553-70c4-4623-be04-995ac03fca2a\" />\n\nFor `<select multiple>`:\n\nChrome:\n\n<img height=\"250\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a7ac52be-d9a4-400a-838a-7df8d201d78a\" />\n\n<img height=\"250\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f839d3f5-366c-4c7e-9d05-94d69af9d38b\" />\n\n<img height=\"250\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0ca629e3-d9c3-47df-a40b-40b667020e48\" />\n\nFirefox:\n\n<img height=\"250\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/bcd47b72-982f-42af-9f8d-568f9789ac68\" />\n\n<img height=\"250\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f3104230-b66a-406f-a434-82158937fda7\" />\n\nFor other test cases, please see the test page: https://codepen.io/sb3nder/full/vExgzbV .\n",
